{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. You're in the recovery unit after your tracheostomy tube exchange. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hey, thanks. I’m a bit groggy, but okay. My throat feels sore, and my neck is tender around the trach site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. You had a flexible bronchoscopy and balloon dilation to help with the stenosis, then we changed your trach tube from fenestrated to unfenestrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, the fenestrated one was making it harder to breathe lately. Did they see much blockage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, there was some granulation tissue and narrowing. They used a balloon to dilate the area and cleaned it out. The new tube should help with airflow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been having more trouble speaking and breathing with the old one. Was the procedure safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You tolerated it very well. No complications. We’re keeping you for a few days to monitor your breathing and pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about my arm? It’s swollen and red near the IV site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed that. It’s likely superficial thrombophlebitis—irritation from the IV. No sign of a blood clot, but we’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not dangerous. It’s uncomfortable but common. We’ll monitor it, and it should improve. No fever or infection signs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’ll watch it. Can I go back on my regular meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve continued your home medications—albuterol, fluticasone, omeprazole, gabapentin, and fluoxetine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. The gabapentin helps with the chronic pain, but the soreness now is worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll add a low-dose oxycodone for breakthrough pain, just for a few days. You can take it every six hours as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’d help. I don’t want to overuse it, but the pain is pretty constant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep it short-term. Your breathing is stable—97% on room air. We did a chest X-ray to check for any issues like pneumothorax, and everything looked clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2169-05-07 19:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2169-05-08 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. How’d you sleep? We checked your lungs this morning—still some crackles at the bases, likely atelectasis. Nothing concerning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2169-05-08 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I slept okay. The pain’s better with the meds. What’s atelectasis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2169-05-08 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It means some small airways are collapsed. Common after sedation. We’ll keep encouraging deep breathing and nebulizers to help open them up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2169-05-08 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll keep doing my pulmonary hygiene."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2169-05-08 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. The speech team also came by to assess you for a speaking valve, but you couldn’t tolerate it due to increased breathing effort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2169-05-08 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, it felt like I was working too hard. Maybe later?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2169-05-08 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll discuss that with interventional pulmonology at your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2169-05-08 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Any word on the bronchial wash results?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2169-05-08 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The gram stain showed normal mouth flora and some white blood cells, but no serious infection. No bacteria like staph were dominant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2169-05-08 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no antibiotics needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2169-05-08 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. Since there’s no sign of infection, we’re holding off. We’ll watch your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2169-05-09 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an ultrasound on your arm this morning to check for a clot. Good news—it ruled out DVT. Just superficial inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2169-05-09 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. The redness hasn’t spread, so that’s good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2169-05-09 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s already looking better. We’ll keep the oxycodone available, but you’re doing well with pain control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2169-05-09 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve only taken it twice yesterday. Mostly using the gabapentin and Tylenol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2169-05-09 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Your oxygen levels are stable, and you’re walking independently. We’re thinking you can go home tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2169-05-09 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2169-05-09 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep an eye on your trach site for redness, swelling, or increased secretions. Watch your arm too—if it gets worse, let us know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2169-05-09 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my breathing—if it gets harder?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2169-05-09 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially if you’re more short of breath or need more nebulizers. Otherwise, keep up with your meds and pulmonary care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2169-05-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. We’re sending you with a short supply of oxycodone for pain, just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2169-05-10 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’ll follow up with interventional pulmonology, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2169-05-10 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’ll coordinate your next trach check. Keep taking your regular meds, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2169-05-10 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2169-05-10 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2169-05-10 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—should I avoid lifting with my right arm?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2169-05-10 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just for a few days. Light activity is fine, but avoid heavy lifting until the redness is gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2169-05-10 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll take it easy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2169-05-10 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’ve done really well. We’re confident you’ll continue to improve at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2169-05-10 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2169-05-10 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2169-05-10 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2169-05-07 19:38:00",
    "admission_end": "2169-05-10 17:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A young woman with a history of bronchopulmonary dysplasia, laryngeal stenosis, and tracheostomy dependence was admitted for post-operative monitoring after a scheduled tracheostomy tube exchange. She underwent flexible bronchoscopy with balloon dilation and exchange from a fenestrated to an unfenestrated Portex 8 trach tube due to progressive shortness of breath and discomfort. The procedure was uncomplicated, and she tolerated it well. Post-operatively, she developed mild right forearm erythema and swelling at the IV site, which was evaluated with ultrasound and determined to be superficial thrombophlebitis without DVT. Pain was managed with a short course of low-dose oxycodone in addition to her home regimen. She was unable to tolerate a speaking valve due to increased work of breathing. Her respiratory status remained stable, and she was discharged home with instructions to continue her chronic medications and follow up with interventional pulmonology.",
    "problems": [
      "Stenosis of larynx",
      "Bronchopulmonary dysplasia originating in the perinatal period",
      "Phlebitis and thrombophlebitis of other sites",
      "Encounter for attention to tracheostomy",
      "Unspecified asthma, uncomplicated",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
